1.0.0 (2026-09-19)
- Finalized the repository package for the merged TypeScript main branch after PR #113: all storage filenames now use uppercase stems with lowercase extensions while device `pipboy` paths remain uppercase.
- Converted Caravan repository source to the PR #113 TypeScript layout under storage/.
- Added concrete local TYPES.d.ts contracts for Caravan's lazy Engine, Renderer, audio, menu, Results, and preview modules.
- Kept all 30 device-facing HOLO/CARAVAN paths unchanged; generated JavaScript is now a build artifact rather than committed source.
- Conversion is type-only for the 16 readable runtime modules: after type erasure, each module matches the existing hardware-tested JavaScript behavior.
- Removed APPINFO/CARAVAN.info from repository source because the TypeScript-era installer/build flow generates installation metadata.
- Version remains Caravan v1.0.0.

2026-09-19 - Cody cleanup, hardware-compatible
- Applied Cody's PR cleanup style to metadata/README organization without changing the tested Caravan runtime.
- Preserved root APP.MIN.JS, APPINFO/CARAVAN.info, and readable root source files because the direct Pip-Boy hardware-test loader requires the known-good 53-file layout.
- Kept Engine-resident / Audio-resident menu-cycle stability fix unchanged; Renderer remains the only large gameplay module unloaded for the compact post-game menu.
- Development logging folder remains local-only and must not be included in the eventual public PR.


v1.0.0 - 2026-09-19
- Deferred Results -> Back cleanup until after the Results knob callback fully returns, then unload/GC/defrag before loading the compact Caravan menu. This targets the fixed ~106-block loss that occurs only on Back-to-menu cycles while pure Rematch remains flat.
- Menu-cycle stability: fully clear exclusive knob listener properties and sever post-game menu callback references before returning to gameplay.
- Targets the exact ~106-block loss observed once per Results -> Caravan menu -> Play cycle while leaving the now-flat Rematch runtime unchanged.
Caravan v1.0.0 - menu suspend headroom fix
- Keep the stable persistent outer Game controller and clean audio controller across post-game menu visits.
- Before loading the post-game menu, unload only the large Engine and Renderer modules and hard-defrag.
- Reload Engine/Renderer lazily on the next Play while reusing the same idled audio controller, avoiding the old ~106-block audio-module cycle leak.
- No changes to card sound bytes/settings, gameplay rules, Results, Game Over Win, betting, or zero-cap behavior.

Caravan v1.0.0 - lean post-game shell stability fix
- Keep the proven persistent match runtime and clean card-audio path unchanged.
- Revert the split-menu routing out of the always-resident APP so live gameplay regains the headroom from the stable build.
- APP now makes only one small choice: initial full menu or lightweight post-game shell.
- Move Play/Bet, Demo, Volume, Rules, and Back routing into CARAVAN_RETURN_MENU so that logic exists only while the post-game menu is open.
- Keep the post-game shell at ~3.1 KB and lazy-load the separate ~2.6 KB Bet/Deck module only when Play Caravan is selected.
- Preserve the player-zero and opponent-zero reset popup paths and 500/500 reset behavior.
- Fix one installed low-memory main-menu mangle typo where the ante-limit helper referenced an undefined `funds` identifier when player funds were below opponent funds.
- No changes to Game rules, Engine, Renderer, clean Play/Discard audio, Game Over Win, Results, or persistent rematch cleanup.

Caravan v1.0.0 - split post-game menu memory fix
- Keep the persistent match runtime that proved flat across consecutive rematches.
- Stop eval-loading the 6.7 KB all-in-one Caravan menu after Results.
- Add a 1.9 KB post-game main-menu shell with the same visible main choices and Rules screen.
- Add a separate 2.6 KB Bet/Deck/Reset module that loads only when Play Caravan is selected from the post-game menu.
- Preserve exact 0-cap reset messages and behavior in the split Bet/Deck module.
- Keep the original full menu unchanged for initial holotape entry.
- Demo/Tutorial and Volume Adjustment remain lazy-loaded only when selected.
- No changes to gameplay rules, persistent Engine/Renderer/Audio behavior, card SFX, Game Over Win, Results, or match cleanup.

Caravan v1.0.0 - low-memory menu runtime fix
- Keep the proven persistent match runtime unchanged: repeated rematches continue reusing Engine, Renderer, and Audio while releasing all per-match data and the 2.5 KB card SFX buffer.
- Keep the post-Results hard defrag before returning to the Caravan menu.
- Reduce the installed CARAVAN_MENU_INTERFACE.MIN.JS runtime from 9,838 bytes to 6,692 bytes by shortening private identifiers only.
- Preserve the menu logic, visible text, betting/deck flow, Demo/Tutorial, Rules/Controls, Volume Adjustment, both zero-cap reset paths, and Play handoff unchanged.
- No changes to gameplay rules, card audio, Game Over Win, Results audio, renderer, engine, or persistent match lifecycle.

Caravan v1.0.0 - menu-return hard-defrag stability fix
- Keep the proven leak-free persistent match runtime used by Rematch and menu-return Play.
- After Results fully unwinds, run one hard E.defrag() before reading/evaluating the full Caravan menu.
- This targets the plain MEMORY crash seen after DATAFREE F1038 when returning to the menu with the reusable Engine/Renderer/Audio modules still resident.
- No changes to game rules, card audio, Game Over Win, Results, betting state, zero-cap behavior, or match runtime cleanup.

Caravan v1.0.0 - menu-return persistent runtime stability fix
- Hardware logs proved Rematch is now stable: G1/G2/G3 all returned to the exact same DATAFREE F1036.
- The remaining ~105-block loss happened only after Results -> Back -> Caravan menu -> Play, when the stable game controller was fully destroyed and recreated.
- Results -> Back now leaves the already-cleaned game controller dormant while the Caravan menu is open; selecting Play reuses the same controller, matching the stable rematch lifecycle.
- Finished-match data is still released before Results: decks/hands/caravans/render state are cleared and audio idle stops music, closes CARAVAN_SFX.BIN, and releases the 2.5 KB SFX buffer.
- Final holotape exit still performs a full game-runtime removal.
- No changes to card audio bytes/settings, Game Over Win, Results, Joker/face-card rules, betting, or either 0-cap terminal state.


Caravan v1.0.0 - Persistent Match Runtime Stability Fix
- Reuses the stateless game Engine and Renderer across matches instead of eval-loading them every game.
- Reuses the clean in-game audio controller across matches while idle() still stops music, closes the SFX bank, and releases the 2.5 KB card buffer after every result.
- Attaches the existing game knob handlers directly instead of eval-loading the tiny Controls wrapper each match.
- Per-match decks, hands, caravans, direction arrays, render state, and card-audio buffer are still released/rebuilt normally.
- Final holotape removal still fully destroys Engine/Renderer/Audio resources.
- Results -> Back and both terminal zero-cap exits also fully release the persistent match runtime before returning to the Caravan menu.
- No card-sound data, ADPCM settings, game rules, Results behavior, or zero-cap behavior changed.
Caravan v1.0.0 - persistent match controller / repeated-game leak fix
- Keep one lightweight CARAVAN_GAME controller alive for the whole Caravan holotape session instead of eval-loading a new outer game controller after every match.
- Heavy Engine, Renderer, Audio, decks, hands, caravans, and render state are still fully released before Game Over Win / Results.
- Rematch, New Opponent, and returning through either zero-cap reset path rebuild only the heavy match modules inside the existing controller.
- Skip CARAVAN_VOLUME_APPLY eval-loading when the requested background-music level is already applied.
- Release the Game Over Win callback reference before entering Results.
- No changes to Caravan rules, card engine, Game startup defrag sequence, audio formats, Results behavior, or either zero-cap state.

Caravan v1.0.0 - repeated-match handoff cleanup fix
- Break the menu -> APP start callback reference immediately after the one-shot game handoff.
- Reclaim only temporary APP game-source/eval objects after the game factory is created and before its existing boot timer runs.
- Leaves the game module's established startup/defrag sequence, gameplay, both zero-cap states, Results, audio, and aggressive post-match cleanup unchanged.

