Caravan v1.0.0 opponent roster test - 2026-09-15
- Added all 14 Fallout: New Vegas Caravan players to the real-match randomized opponent pool.
- Results now offers Rematch, Challenge New Opponent, and Back.
- Rematch preserves the current opponent; Challenge New Opponent selects a different player and reuses the resident game runtime instead of reloading Engine/Renderer/Audio.
- Kept Tutorial fixed to Ringo.
Caravan v1.0.0 - 2026-09-13
- Removed the custom screen-off/wake-resume system and all Caravan `Pip.wakeUp`/framebuffer/LCD interception. Manual Power sleep now follows stock firmware behavior and does not preserve a live match.
- Disabled automatic idle sleep only while a match is active; the user's original idle timeout is restored on every game cleanup path.
- Removed the game's suspended/pending wake state and gameplay-audio suspend/resume code to reduce resident memory and lifecycle complexity.
- Added stronger game/menu/results transition cleanup with reference release, garbage collection, and defragmentation before loading the next large module.
- Replaced the gameplay codec-reset start/stop hack with direct DAC power/output initialization when supported by firmware.
- Kept Playing Card and Discard as one-time cached ADPCM buffers with no per-card bank reads or retry loops.
- Kept readable source identifiers human-friendly; short identifiers are reserved for intentionally minified runtime files.
- Re-minified the installed APP.JS runtime identifiers aggressively after the reviewer-facing cleanup so descriptive source names do not consume extra Espruino memory during match launch.
- Removed the pre-launch full-screen clear; the renderer now clears only when the game has successfully reached its first draw, preventing a failed/low-memory launch from leaving a permanent black screen.
- Removed manual DAC power/mode forcing between Results and Rematch; audio now resets through the normal Pip audio API to prevent stale/scratchy SFX after idle result screens.

- Added invisible every-match Rematch cleanup/defrag and permanent opening-complete state to prevent late 5-to-4 hand regression.
- Added a file-audio roundabout diagnostic after the third-match scratch survived both every-match cleanup and `Pip.initDAC()`.
- Playing Card and Discard now materialize their exact selected-volume gameplay slices as tiny WAV files and play through `Pip.audioStart()`; no custom gameplay `audioStartVar()` path remains.
- Bottle-cap Results audio now uses a normal WAV file instead of custom variable-audio queue pumping.
- Temporarily disabled active-match Lazy Days playback for the three-match long-Rematch isolation test; music preview/settings are retained.
- Removed the failed native DAC reset from Rematch; normal cleanup/defrag remains.

Test build note (2026-09-14):
- File-audio roundabout Play/Discard WAVs now retain one quiet ADPCM block before and after each active effect to remove the low click/thump heard at card playback startup/shutdown.
- CARD_SFX.APPLIED marker schema advanced so existing generated WAVs are rebuilt automatically.

