- Play/Discard stream in 256-byte native ADPCM blocks over continuous music.
- One flat 256-byte block is reserved between callbacks; no full card SFX is resident.
- Renderer is released before Results and reloaded only on Rematch.

- Test rules pass: Disband Caravan action, opening discard/redraw, deck-exhaustion loss, tutorial/rules updates.
- Increased the readability of the small top-left rank/letter text on placed caravan cards only, while keeping the larger suit art clear and avoiding overlap.
- Reduced the placed-card corner rank/letter enlargement to a middle-size treatment after hardware readability testing; hand cards and suit graphics remain unchanged.
- Reworked placed-card top-left rank rendering to be crisp and readable instead of overdrawn/blurry, while keeping hand cards unchanged.
- Trimmed the crisp placed-card top-left rank rendering by about 2 pixels while keeping the cleaner sharp look.
- Added "Will Be Applied In-Game" notes beside the Sound Effects and Background Music headings in Volume Adjustment.
- Matched the full Volume Adjustment heading notes to the same Monofonto16 font and size as SOUND EFFECTS and BACKGROUND MUSIC.
- Added zero-funds Caravan bankroll handling: rematch/challenge lockout, highlighted reset flow back to 500 total funds, and hard bet caps so wagers can never exceed available funds.
- Zero-cap Results now has exactly one highlighted option in every result path: "Not enough bottle caps to play...EXIT GAME!"; no separate Back option is shown.
- Reset Total Ante popup now overlays the CARAVAN - BET screen instead of clearing the full display, leaving the Play Caravan background visible around the popup.
- Centered the highlighted "Reset Total Ante" text horizontally inside the RESET popup.
- Added a live opponent bankroll: opponents now start at 500 caps, gain/lose the exact wager opposite the player, can reach 1000 if they win the player's full 500, and wagers are capped by both sides' remaining caps.
- Restored the bottle-cap graphic on the results screen by reclaiming/defragmenting before the low-memory image load and avoiding the previous over-conservative skip.
- Reset Total Ante now resets both the player and the current opponent bankrolls to 500 before returning to the normal bet controls.
- Reduced results-screen cap-image memory usage with a dedicated compact result-cap bank to prevent LOW_MEMORY during later matches.
- Preserved bottle-cap result audio for all loss amounts, including losing the full remaining bankroll.
- Reset Total Ante continues to restore both player and current opponent bankrolls to 500.
Development fix (2026-09-18): unload the completed Game/Engine/Renderer/Audio runtime before loading Results; rematches reload a fresh game runtime to avoid the winner-transition LOW_MEMORY crash.

- Bottle Cap result/preview audio fully replaced with the supplied Short, Medium, and Long cap WAVs.
- Results timing now matches the new clips: Short = 10 counter steps, Medium = 20, Long = 30; cap audio is explicitly stopped on the final movement step.
- Bottle Cap Preview now uses the supplied Medium clip.

- Dev test: reverted session-resident card-SFX buffer; Game Over Win now explicitly stops/releases firmware audio before Results to prevent per-match heap loss and second-game loading stalls.

2026-09-19 - Multi-match/Joker memory fix
- New matches now use a two-stage teardown/load handoff so old Result/Menu callbacks fully unwind before GC/defrag and game module evaluation.
- Joker and face-card group mutations now compact/insert arrays in place instead of repeated Array.splice allocations.
- Joker performs a garbage collection immediately before its board-wide removal pass.
Cleanup stability test:
- Break APP<->Menu, APP<->Game, and APP<->Results callback reference cycles during teardown.
- Release audio, renderer, engine, render state, decks, hands, caravans, and direction buffers before handing Results back to APP.
- Avoid allocating replacement empty arrays during finished-game cleanup.
- Results now detaches its listener/audio/timers before invoking Rematch/New Opponent/Back.
- Stability: simplified the menu-to-game handoff to a single APP-owned timer chain. The menu now sends the bet state immediately; APP draws LOADING GAME, tears down the old screen on the next tick, reclaims memory, and starts the game. This removes the duplicate loading-animation timer/callback relay that could leave later matches stuck on LOADING GAME even with ample free memory.
- Restored the direct, hardware-proven menu-to-game startup handoff. Removed the recently-added nested 20 ms game-loader timer while preserving aggressive post-match cleanup and all in-game startup defrags.
1.0.0-stability-cache (2026-09-19)
- Cache only the CARAVAN_GAME_AUDIO factory across matches so repeated matches do not re-evaluate its 1.7 KB runtime source.
- Keep a fresh clean audio instance per match; the original music/SFX controller and resident card-sound buffer lifecycle are unchanged.
- Mangle only private identifiers in the installed CARAVAN_GAME.MIN.JS runtime to reduce its resident source footprint by about 5 KB and preserve gameplay headroom.
- No changes to rules, Results, 0-cap terminal states, card-sound bytes, ADPCM settings, timing, pitch, or volume.

- Hardware-test packaging restored to the last known-good direct-test layout; post-win Results loading is deferred one event turn so the completed win callback can be reclaimed before Results eval.

- Kept the already-loaded game Engine resident across Results -> menu -> Play cycles; hardware A/B testing showed the fixed ~106-block loss persisted when only Engine was re-evaluated, while pure rematches stayed flat.
- Menu suspension now unloads only Renderer (plus per-match data already released) while preserving Engine and the idled clean Audio controller; Renderer still supplies the large menu headroom recovery.
- Retained deferred Results Back cleanup so Results fully unwinds before menu suspension/GC.
